# vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/options/__init__.py

Public surface of the options package (model, graph and subagent-spec builders). Importing it also registers a process-wide `openai` provider profile with the `deepagents` library, so a bare-string OpenAI model that skips `build_model` gets the same transport defaults.

Source: `vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/options/__init__.py` (lines 1-59)
Executor: code
Called from: `vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/client.py` and `vvaharness/backends/llm/deepagents.py` (imports `build_model`, `build_model_cached`, `build_oneshot_options`, `build_streaming_agent`, `release_session`, `resumable`, `get_subagent_specs`)

// src: vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/options/__init__.py:36-49
// Runs once, at import time.
register_provider_profile("openai", ProviderProfile(init_kwargs={
  use_responses_api: true,
  store: false,
  include: ["reasoning.encrypted_content"],   // model_building.RESPONSES_INCLUDE_ENCRYPTED_REASONING
  timeout: MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS             // limits.MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 1800.0 seconds
}))   // external: deepagents.register_provider_profile
// preserved: the timeout here is NOT effort-scaled (build_model scales it per effort tier); the source says a bare-string model has no effort tier at registration time.

